🌱 EcoProof
Real-Time Environmental Monitoring & Emissions Tracking System

EcoProof is a real-time environmental monitoring system that tracks industrial emissions and air quality data, detects anomalies, and provides transparent dashboards for public awareness and administrative action.

It combines data analytics, anomaly detection, blockchain logging, and interactive dashboards to promote environmental accountability.

🚀 Features

📡 Real-Time Sensor Data Monitoring

📊 Interactive Public Dashboard (Streamlit)

🛑 Anomaly Detection for Pollution Spikes

🔐 Blockchain-Based Data Logging for Transparency

📈 Visual Pollution Trends & AQI Analysis

📂 CSV Upload & Data Processing

🛠️ Tech Stack

Frontend & Dashboard: Streamlit

Backend: Python

Data Processing: Pandas

Visualization: Plotly

Blockchain Logging: Custom Python Blockchain

Deployment: Streamlit Cloud / Local Deployment

📂 Project Structure
EcoProof/
│
├── public_dashboard.py        # Public pollution monitoring dashboard
├── admin_dashboard.py         # Admin monitoring & logging dashboard
├── anomaly_model.py           # Pollution anomaly detection logic
├── blockchain.py              # Custom blockchain implementation
├── data/
│   └── blockchain_data.json   # Stored blockchain records
│
└── README.md
📊 How It Works

Sensors generate environmental data (CO, NO₂, SO₂, PM2.5, PM10, AQI, etc.).

Data is uploaded via CSV.

The anomaly detection model checks for pollution threshold violations.

New data entries are logged securely using blockchain.

Dashboards display real-time trends and alerts.

⚙️ Installation & Setup
1️⃣ Clone the Repository
git clone https://github.com/your-username/ecoproof.git
cd ecoproof
2️⃣ Install Dependencies
pip install -r requirements.txt
3️⃣ Run the Public Dashboard
streamlit run public_dashboard.py
4️⃣ Run the Admin Dashboard
streamlit run admin_dashboard.py
📈 Sample Data Format

Your CSV file should contain columns like:

timestamp, sensor_id, plant_name, plant_id,
co_level, no2_level, so2_level,
pm2_5, pm10, o3_level,
temperature, humidity,
wind_speed, wind_direction,
aqi, pollution_score, anomaly_flag
